MackTuesday was wandering thru a dungeon and left this note in a bottle 
in a fountain:
> I'm playing the latest vanilla version.
> 
> This game is the first I've played in which I was able to complete both
> the Sokoban levels and the Gnomish mines.  
> 
> I want to read blessed scrolls of identify until I get that big lucky
> break.  ... I have only two more identify scrolls at my disposal, both cursed. Is this even an important goal right now? 

No, this is not an important goal for a Barbarian IMHO. Make a stash, 
come back later

> I also have some nice, but damaged, pieces of armor: a +4 cloak
> (orcish?), +3 elven boots, and a +2 helmet.  The cloak and boots are
> burnt; the cloak is down to +3.  The helmet is thoroughly rusty.  I
> haven't found any oil so far.  Is it possible to repair them?

Yes, but for a non-magical character, the repair is not worth the 
expense. There are better cloaks and head protection to be found; the 
boots will do until you find a pair of boots which will speed your progress.

> I'm guessing that grease would protect the helmet for the future, right?
> How can I protect the burnable items?  
Yes; and burnable armor requires magical enchantments of a sort.
What's the best way to deal with
> pyrolisks?  (I just want a hint for the last question.)

Those monsters which can only see their own reflection cannot gaze upon you.
> 
> My large cat has died. Should I bother getting a new one?  I know of a polymorph
> trap and I can obtain a leash.  Are there any interesting possibilities
> there?

Yes and yes. Having a friend, or two, to watch your back is always useful.
> 
> I ate a troll corpse.  Did that do me any good, other than keeping it
> from reanimating?
Maybe, if you are lucky. What can trolls do which others cannot? You 
might "pick up" something.
> 
> 
> Are there any monsters that can loot a locked chest or box?

No, but they might engulf and digest it.
> 
> Finally, would anyone like to give me a general plan of action for the
> near future?
> 
If you can't kill it, run away.
If you can kill from a distance, do so.
Keep your friends close and your enemies at a distance.
Most items of gear which are useful and necessary at this early stage in 
the game will be replaced by a better item later. Don't become too 
attached to common weapons and armor. Yes, you have common weapons and 
armor.
If you haven't killed the priest in Minetown, chat with him. He has 
things to offer...for the right price.



